<h1>6. EMPIRICAL BENCHMARKING &amp; TEST RESULTS</h1>

<h2>6.1 End-to-End Automated Test Verification</h2>
<p>
The system was verified via an automated PowerShell test harness:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Authentication Verified:</strong> <code>POST /api/auth/login</code> for <code>cashier1</code> returned HTTP 200 OK with valid JWT bearer token.</li>
  <li><strong>Catalog Retrieval:</strong> 8 seeded products retrieved across 4 categories.</li>
  <li><strong>Target Product:</strong> <code>BEV-002</code> ("Organic Green Tea 500ml") initial stock: <strong>4 units</strong> (Threshold: 5).</li>
  <li><strong>Checkout Execution:</strong> Sold 1 unit. Stored procedure generated invoice <code>INV-20261002-0001</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Stock Deduction:</strong> Stock was decremented from <strong>4 to 3 units</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>SignalR Alert Trigger:</strong> Because <code>3 &lt;= 5</code>, <code>ReceiveLowStockAlert</code> was dispatched to all screens.</li>
  <li><strong>Revenue Aggregation:</strong> Dashboard revenue updated by <code>+$3.41</code> immediately.</li>
</ol>

