<h1>7. CONCLUSION &amp; FUTURE ROADMAP</h1>
<p>
The <strong>Real-Time Inventory &amp; Billing System</strong> proves that modern WPF MVVM and classic Windows Forms desktop applications can be seamlessly harmonized with ASP.NET Core Web API microservices and SQL Server database engines. Replacing polling with bi-directional SignalR WebSockets and enforcing pessimistic row locks eliminates race conditions and provides sub-second responsiveness.
</p>

<h3>Future Enhancements:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Offline Resilient Queueing:</strong> Local SQLite queuing with automated cloud sync on reconnection.</li>
  <li><strong>Hardware ESC/POS Printing:</strong> Direct raw byte ESC/POS printer support over serial/USB ports.</li>
  <li><strong>Machine Learning Demand Forecasting:</strong> Predictive inventory reordering models based on sales velocity.</li>
</ul>

